  "description": "Part conversion of ground floor retail unit into cafe (Use class E); single storey front extension; single storey side to rear extension to No.1 Byron Road; single storey outbuilding in rear garden to No.3 Byron Road",
  "development_type": "Minor retail and service",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The introduction of a shopfront along Christchurch Avenue is inappropriate due to its location outside of a shopping frontage in a local centre. The proposal is therefore contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 of The London Plan (2021), Policy GR1 and GR8 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed single storey rear extension, by reason of its excessive rearward projection, is unduly obtrusive, results in overshadowing and loss of outlook, and would be detrimental to the visual and residential amenities of the occupiers of the host property at No 3&amp;nbsp;Byron Road, contrary to the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3.D 7 of The London Plan (2021), Policy GR1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041) and the adopted Supplementary Planning Document Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
